{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.StrongMultiplicativity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.StrongMultiplicativity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Flatness"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.formal_group_is_filtered_bialgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.formal_group_is_filtered_bialgebra","kind":"axiom","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L192-L212","doc":"Bridge theorem: the strong multiplicativity result in this module\nimplies `FormalGroups.strong_multiplicativity_holds`.\n\nThe connection is:\n- `NoncommutativeFormalGroup.mul` ↔ multiplication on `AlgElement G k`\n- `NoncommutativeFormalGroup.comul` ↔ `FilteredBialgebra.comul`\n- `GrobnerShirshovBasis.composition_lemma` ↔ `composition_lemma`\n  from `CompositionLemma.lean`\n\nThe bridge requires constructing a `FilteredBialgebra` instance from\na `NoncommutativeFormalGroup` and its associated `GrobnerShirshovBasis`.\nThis construction is axiomatised since it depends on the specific\nformal group law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.frobenius_preserved_by_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.frobenius_preserved_by_degree","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L168-L188","doc":"The Frobenius relation is preserved under the GS deformation:\ngiven a filtered bialgebra structure on `Dist(G)`, the identity\n`Δ(xy) = Δ(x) · Δ(y)` holds at every filtration degree.\n\nThis is the degree-by-degree version of strong multiplicativity.\nThe proof proceeds by induction on filtration degree `n`:\n- Base case `n = 0`: `F₀` contains only scalars, where `Δ` is\n  trivially multiplicative.\n- Inductive step: assume `Δ` is multiplicative on `F_{n-1}`.\n  For `x ∈ Fₙ \\ F_{n-1}`, write `x` in GS normal form.\n  The normal form has leading term in degree `n` and lower-order\n  terms in `F_{n-1}`.  By the inductive hypothesis and the\n  generator-level computation, `Δ(xy) = Δ(x)·Δ(y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.tensor_gs_basis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.tensor_gs_basis","kind":"axiom","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L117-L134","doc":"A GS basis for `k⟨G⟩/(Σ)` induces a GS basis on the tensor product\n`k⟨G⟩/(Σ) ⊗ k⟨G⟩/(Σ)` under the tensor order.\n\nThe proof checks that:\n1. S-polynomials within `Σ₁` or `Σ₂` reduce to zero (by the base GS property).\n2. S-polynomials between `Σᵢ` and commutativity relations reduce to zero\n   (the commutativity relations have no overlap with `Σᵢ` since they\n   involve generators from different copies).\n3. S-polynomials among commutativity relations reduce to zero (trivially,\n   since commutativity relations don't overlap with each other). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.tensorRewritingSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.tensorRewritingSystem","kind":"axiom","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L103-L115","doc":"The tensor product rewriting system: given a GS basis for `k⟨G⟩/(Σ)`,\nthe tensor product `k⟨G⟩/(Σ) ⊗ k⟨G⟩/(Σ)` is presented by the\nrewriting system on `k⟨G₁ ⊔ G₂⟩` with:\n- Relations `Σ₁` (the original relations acting on `G₁` generators)\n- Relations `Σ₂` (the original relations acting on `G₂` generators)\n- Commutativity relations `g₁ · g₂ = g₂ · g₁` for all `g₁ ∈ G₁`, `g₂ ∈ G₂`\n\nThe commutativity relations ensure that `G₁` and `G₂` generators\ncommute, which is the defining property of the tensor product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.tensorOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.tensorOrder","kind":"axiom","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L84-L101","doc":"The admissible order on `TensorGen G` induced by a base order on `G`.\n\nThe tensor product order on `k⟨G₁ ⊔ G₂⟩` is the deg-lex extension:\nfirst compare by total degree (word length), then lexicographically\nusing `Sum.inl < Sum.inr` between components and the base order `ord`\nwithin each component.\n\nAxiomatised because constructing a well-founded deg-lex order on\n`List (G ⊕ G)` from `ord : AdmissibleOrder G` requires a decidable\nlinear order on `G ⊕ G` and the well-foundedness proof for the\nlexicographic product, which needs `Fintype G` or an explicit\nenumeration.  The result is standard: every admissible order on `G`\nlifts to an admissible order on `G ⊕ G` via the coproduct ordering.\n\nReference: Bokut & Chen, Bull. Math. Sci. 4 (2014), §2.1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instDecidableEqTensorGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.instDecidableEqTensorGen","kind":"instance","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L81-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.TensorGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.TensorGen","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L71-L79","doc":"Generators for the tensor product algebra `k⟨G⟩ ⊗ k⟨G⟩`.\n\nThe tensor product `k⟨G⟩ ⊗ k⟨G⟩` is isomorphic to the quotient of\nthe free algebra `k⟨G₁ ⊔ G₂⟩` on two disjoint copies of `G` by the\nideal generated by `g₁ · g₂ − g₂ · g₁` for `g₁ ∈ G₁`, `g₂ ∈ G₂`.\n\nWe represent `G₁ ⊔ G₂` as `G ⊕ G` (the sum type). The `Sum.inl`\ncopy represents `g ⊗ 1` and `Sum.inr` represents `1 ⊗ g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.comul_is_alg_hom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.comul_is_alg_hom","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L66-L66","doc":"`Δ` is an algebra homomorphism: `Δ(xy) = Δ(x) · Δ(y)`.\nThis is the **Frobenius relation** / strong multiplicativity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.tensor_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.tensor_mul","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The tensor product multiplication `(A ⊗ A) × (A ⊗ A) → A ⊗ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.comul_filtered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.comul_filtered","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Comultiplication respects the filtration:\n`x ∈ Fₙ ⟹ Δ(x) ∈ ⊕_{i+j≤n} Fᵢ ⊗ Fⱼ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.tensor_filt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.tensor_filt","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The tensor product has its own filtration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.counit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.counit","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Counit `ε : A → k` (represented as A → A for simplicity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.comul","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Comultiplication `Δ : A → A ⊗ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.toAlgebraFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra.toAlgebraFiltration","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L51-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FilteredBialgebra","kind":"structure","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/StrongMultiplicativity.lean#L45-L67","doc":"A **filtered bialgebra**: an algebra `A` with a compatible filtration\nand a comultiplication `Δ : A → A ⊗ A` that respects the filtration.\n\nWe model `A ⊗ A` abstractly as a separate type `T` with a\nmultiplication, rather than using pairs (which incorrectly model\n`A × A` rather than `A ⊗ A`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}